# Root .gitignore -- ALLOWLIST. Ignore everything, then re-admit by name.
# Fails CLOSED: a folder nobody thought about stays private by default.
#
# Installed 2026-08-12, replacing the 2026-07-28 secrets-only version, as
# part of collapsing carolus_repo/ into a single repo rooted here. See
# research-log/01-projet/plan-restructuration-repo.md for the full plan and
# research-log/01-projet/audit-systeme-fichiers.md for what stays private
# and why.

# 1. Ignore every top-level entry.
/*

# 2. Re-admit only what is published.
!/carolus_ws/
!/shortcuts/
!/overleaf/
!/README.md
!/LICENSE
!/NOTICE
!/.gitignore
# Added 2026-08-20: the self-contained ROS2 port (lab PC + Raspberry Pi 5),
# its own manual and its own copy of the detection/solver core. Published
# because it is meant to be handed over and built by someone else -- that
# portability is the whole reason the folder exists.
!/raspberry5-carolus-ros2/

# .env.example is NOT published: it documents this project's internal
# Tavily/Perplexity research workflow (research-log/09-tavily/...), which
# itself is not published -- the file would be an orphaned pointer to a
# reader who has no research-log/. Kept on disk locally, just not tracked.
.env.example

# 3. Inside those, exclude what must not travel.
#    (Migrated from sync_repo.sh's --exclude flags, which is retired by
#    this restructure.)

# Build output -- regenerable
carolus_ws/build/
carolus_ws/devel/
carolus_ws/build_isolated/
carolus_ws/devel_isolated/
carolus_ws/logs/
# colcon's own output dir, created when a ROS2 build was run from here
# (2026-08-19). Singular "log", distinct from catkin's "logs" above.
carolus_ws/log/
# colcon build output inside the ROS2 folder, same reasoning
raspberry5-carolus-ros2/build/
raspberry5-carolus-ros2/install/
raspberry5-carolus-ros2/log/

# Upstream clone, not ours to vendor
carolus_ws/src/robot_localization/

# Absolute symlink into /opt/ros on this machine -- meaningless elsewhere
/carolus_ws/src/CMakeLists.txt

# Session logs -- robot telemetry, no value to a reader
shortcuts/logs/

# Python / editor noise
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.swp
*.swo

# Secrets -- defence in depth; none are expected in the published set
.env
.env.*
*.key
*.pem

# overleaf/README.md (editorial notes about the main.tex draft) points at
# research-log/, which is not published -- it would be a dead reference to a
# reader. main.tex itself was in this same block until 2026-08-27, when the
# user explicitly chose to track it despite the same issue (CLAUDE.md, "Two
# LaTeX documents" section) -- that decision is deliberate, do not re-add it
# here to "fix" it back.
overleaf/README.md

# No compiled PDF is tracked for any of the three LaTeX documents -- user
# decision, 2026-08-27. A reader with the repo compiles their own.
# overleaf/technical.pdf was tracked before this date; it was untracked
# (git rm --cached), not deleted. Named explicitly rather than a blanket
# *.pdf, which would also catch overleaf/figures/carolus-frames.pdf -- a
# source asset \includegraphics-ed into technical.tex, not a compiled
# output, and it must stay tracked for the manual to compile at all.
overleaf/technical.pdf
overleaf/main.pdf
raspberry5-carolus-ros2/technical-ros2.pdf

# LaTeX intermediates: keep .tex sources, drop the rest
*.aux
*.log
*.out
*.toc
*.synctex.gz

# Exception to *.log above, deliberately narrow. These four files are the only
# recording that exists of the BUG-141 twisted-pair ambiguity and of the
# cheirality fix working -- 1469 poses before, 3037 after, taken 2026-09-04 on
# the Pi 5. No further hardware sessions are planned, so they cannot be
# re-recorded. Scoped to this one dataset folder on purpose: do NOT widen it to
# raspberry5-carolus-ros2/data/ generally, or the next rosbag lands in git.
!raspberry5-carolus-ros2/data/bug141_square_2026-09-04/*.log
